		<h3><strong class="gg">Perks - Abilities</strong></h3>
		<p>
			Each player has access to a range of abilities, which you can read about by typing !perk
		</p>
		<p>
			It might be a bit difficult to understand at first, but it's worth it, the admin promises!
		</p>
		<br/>
		<h3><strong class="gg">Endgame Collapse</strong></h3>
		<p>
			The final sprint to the safe room! When the survivors are close to the safe room, the military begins clearing the surrounding area,
		</p>
		<p>
			a countdown to bombardment begins - you need to make it to the safe room in one piece and fend off the horde!
		</p>
		<br/>
		<h3><strong class="gg">Perk Effects:</strong></h3>
		<p>
			Perks can apply <strong class="chat">Positive</strong> and <strong>Negative</strong> effects.
		</p>
		<br/>
		<hr/>
		<br/>
		<p>
			<strong class="chat">Rage</strong> - Anyone who deals damage to you will be knocked back, and your attacks will speed up!
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong class="chat">Persistence</strong> - Reduces incoming damage from enemies by a certain percentage.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong class="chat">Haste</strong> - Increases movement speed by a certain percentage. </p>
		<p>
			<strong class="chat">Endurance</strong> - This effect can save you from being incapacitated.
		</p>
		<br/>
		<hr/>
		<br/>
		<p>
			<strong>Hindered</strong> - Reduces movement speed by a certain percentage.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Exposed</strong> - Increases damage taken. Removed after healing or getting hurt.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Poisoning</strong> - Permanent health under this effect is converted to temporary health.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Exhausted</strong> - Prevents the use of certain perks, such as "Sprinter".
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Deep Wound</strong> - You'll gradually bleed out and fall soon, regardless of HP.
		</p>
